earing is printed as ''similar to the Battle Cat, only +10% to pinpoint and identify sounds and to track/locate by sound''; the Battle Cat figures (80% +2% per level from printed 77; 72% +2% per level and the -20% for artificial sounds from printed 78) are restated beside the sentence and no summed percentage is stored, because the book does not print one. || SKILLS: Speaks American at 80% is Language: Native Tongue 80, per_level 0. Sing 35+15 = 50. Radio: Basic 45+20 = 65. Surveillance Systems is the catalog''s Surveillance, 30+10 = 40. Intelligence 32+10 = 42. Detect Ambush 30+10 = 40. Detect Concealment 25+10 = 35. Land Navigation 36+20 = 56. Wilderness Survival 30+10 = 40. W.P. Knife (Vibro-Blade), W.P. Energy Rifle, one W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Basic (others not available) is the grant plus hand_to_hand costs {} (no style sold). || RELATED: four at level one, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Communications, Domestic, Physical and W.P. any; Espionage +5; Medical First Aid only; Military +5; Rogue any except Computer Hacking, no bonus printed; Technical any (+10%) except Computer Operation and Computer Programming; Wilderness +5; Electrical, Mechanical, Pilot, Pilot Related and Science none. ''Mutants in the service of the CS are never taught to read'' is a restriction line, not an exclusion. SECONDARY: four at level one plus two at each of levels 2, 4, 8 and 12, same lists without bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: ''basically the same as Dog Boys'', then the entry prints its own basic list, which is what is stored: DPM riot armor (dog-pack-dpm-riot-armor), tinted goggles or helmet with a visor (choice), radio as walkie-talkie, flashlight, pocket mirror, 100 ft of lightweight rope as five 20 ft lengths, a net for snaring ground animals and people (choice of net-man-size or net-animal-thrown, judgement), portable language translator, laser distancer as pocket-laser-distancer, three flares, six hand grenades (hand-grenade; the book names no type), three smoke grenades, survival knife, a Vibro-Blade of choice (vibro-knife, vibro-saber, vibro-sword or vibro-claws), C-12 laser rifle or C-14 Fire Breather (choice), backpack, utility belt, air filter, gas mask and canteen. The printed comb is a trivial personal item with no gear row; it is not in equipment_starting. Equipment Available Upon Assignment is not starting equipment and is not stored. || MONEY: the entry prints only a token monthly salary of 70-100 credits with all basic needs provided by the CS military. It says bats are given the same freedoms, privileges and measure of trust as Dog Boys, but prints no starting sum and does not point to the Dog Boy money paragraph, so no starting_money is stored and the salary is a restriction line. || OPTIONAL DOG BOY TABLES: the entry says nothing about them; no restriction line. || Magic: none. Psionics: none. Cybernetics: none. The average weight line prints 100-120 pounds as 45 to 72 kg; stored as printed. Identification coding (the Dog Boys'' dual I.D. system), typical missions (reconnaissance and intelligence), the average bat''s age and level (5-9 years old, 3rd-5th level) and the program numbers (about 240 in service, discontinued) are lore."
---

## Lore

The Mutant Bat is the Lone Star labs'' second small-mammal project: a five foot,
bat-headed humanoid whose arms are the frames of broad membrane wings. The
designers hoped an animal people already feared would make a frightening night
hunter for the Coalition. What they got instead is an agreeable, dependable
soldier that nobody finds very scary.

It flies quietly but not quickly, sees poorly by day, and finds its way in
pitch darkness by echolocation, backed by sharp ears and a good nose. Against
opponents with optics, sensors and energy weapons those gifts count for
little, and the sonar itself can give the bat away, so the program has been
closed. Roughly 240 remain in uniform, scouting by night over the Pecos
Badlands against low-tech raiders and standing guard at Lone Star City and the
Complex. They are on good terms with Dog Boys and the mutant cats, cannot
abide the mutant rats, and will be kept on until they die of old age.

## GM Notes

The stored Spd is the 2D6 ground and climbing speed; roll 6D6+6 separately for
flying speed. The +3 dodge applies only in the air, so it is not added to the
sheet. Hearing is the Battle Cat''s with +10% on the percentages.

The book prints no starting money, only an allowance of 70-100 credits a month,
though bats enjoy the same trust and privileges as Dog Boys and may rise as
high as Lieutenant. Hand to Hand: Basic cannot be upgraded. A typical bat is
5-9 years old and 3rd to 5th level. One outside Coalition service is a feral or
a free-born and is hunted by the CS.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mutant-bat');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mutant-bat';

